---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { htb, htbLine } from '../data/htb';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="A student who breaks things for a grade. Offensive security, Active Directory, and the writeups that come after.">
<!-- ================= OPENING ================= -->
<header class="open">
  <p class="eyebrow">/ About</p>
  <h1 class="lead">
    <span class="ln"><span class="i">A student who</span></span>
    <span class="ln"><span class="i">breaks things</span></span>
    <span class="ln crimson"><span class="i">for a grade.</span></span>
  </h1>
  <span class="slash"></span>
  <p class="lede">My main platform is HackTheBox: <b>{htb.machines} machines</b> across Easy → Insane.
    I write a machine up <b>after it retires</b>, because explaining the chain is where
    the learning actually sticks.</p>
</header>

<!-- ================= VITALS ================= -->
<section class="vitals">
  <div class="vital"><p class="k">Identity</p><p class="v">Certifa</p><p class="d">Mike · 24 y/o</p></div>
  <div class="vital"><p class="k">Location</p><p class="v">Utrecht</p><p class="d">Netherlands</p></div>
  <div class="vital"><p class="k">Studying at</p><p class="v">Hogeschool Utrecht</p><p class="d">Cybersecurity &amp; Cloud BSc</p></div>
  <div class="vital"><p class="k">Primary platform</p><p class="v">HackTheBox</p><p class="d">{htbLine}</p></div>
  <div class="vital"><p class="k">Attack OS</p><p class="v">Kali Linux</p><p class="d">tmux, vim, burp</p></div>
</section>

<!-- ================= PROSE ================= -->
<section class="prose">
  <div class="prose-grid">
    <p class="prose-k">The long version</p>
    <div>
      <p>It started on a <b>Nintendo DS Lite with an R4 card</b>. A flashcart that let the
        console run things Nintendo never approved. I was young enough that I didn't really
        know what I was doing. I just knew the rules turned out to be negotiable. After that
        it was Minecraft servers, CS:GO cheats, Runescape bots, game files pulled apart to
        see what was inside. Different games, same question every time:
        <b>where's the advantage nobody's using</b>.</p>

      <p>Eventually I stopped asking that about games. The family PC and the router at home
        were the first things I broke that weren't a toy, and the interesting part wasn't
        that they broke. It was that <b>it had been possible the whole time</b> and nobody
        had bothered to look.</p>

      <p class="pull">Why know a little when you can know it all.</p>

      <p>The handle doesn't mean anything, by the way. I needed one, <em>Certifa</em> sounded
        right, and it stuck. I'd rather tell you that than invent a story for it.</p>

      <p>None of this is school, either. My course is networking, cloud, enterprise
        infrastructure, automation. Genuinely useful, and it gave me a structure I wouldn't
        have built on my own. But the offensive side happens <b>next to it, on my own time</b>.
        I learn properly when I decide to, and this is the thing I decided to. What I read
        about gets rebuilt at home, on a Windows Server 2022 domain controller and two
        workstations, so a chain I've only read about becomes one I've actually run.
        Anything I do more than twice ends up in Python. <a class="inline" href="https://github.com/Certifa/nmapfullscan" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>nmapfullscan.py</b></a> came out of
        that: sweep every TCP port, parse what actually answered, then run service detection
        on only those. It exists because I got tired of typing the same two commands and
        mis-copying port lists between them.</p>

      <p>Why this and not something easier: it's the same feeling as a boss going down in a
        Souls game. You throw yourself at the same wall for hours, it finally gives, and for
        about thirty seconds you're the best there is. <b>Relief and dopamine in the same
        hit.</b> Then you go looking for the next wall.</p>

      <p>I'm not tidy about it. I move faster than I document. Three steps past a foothold
        before I've written down how I got there, then re-deriving the whole thing later for
        the writeup. I've started taking notes while the box is still open instead of after.
        And I've spent <b>three days on one machine</b> rather than take the hint, which I'd
        call stubbornness if it didn't keep working.</p>

      <p>Which is why the writeups exist. Explaining a chain to someone else is where the
        learning actually sticks, and it's the part most people skip. It's also the honest
        picture of the job: <b>mostly reading, failing, and writing things down</b>. Not a
        hoodie, not a green screen, and not illegal. These are rented machines built to be
        broken.</p>

      <p>The hard part isn't the boxes. It's that almost nobody I know offline understands
        what I do. I come out of a room having got domain admin and it doesn't translate.
        The people who get it are online, and they're a lot of the reason I've kept going.
        And I'm impatient: there are people younger than me with certs and seats, and
        <b>I don't have the seat yet</b>. That keeps me up more than any box does.</p>

      <p>No certifications yet. <b>CJCA</b> is booked, <b>CPTS</b> is next, CCNA after that.
        I'd rather show the work than the paper, but I'm going to have both. What I'm after
        is a <b>first red-team seat</b>: an internship or a junior role, against something
        real, with people better than me in the room. Not famous. Just genuinely good at
        this, and still enjoying it in five years.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= WHAT I ACTUALLY DO ================= -->
<section class="kit">
  <p class="eyebrow">The kit · four things I keep going back to</p>
  <div class="kit-grid">
    <article class="disc"><span class="wipe"></span>
      <p class="n">01</p>
      <h3>Windows /<br>Active Directory</h3>
      <ul><li>Kerberoasting &amp; AS-REP</li><li>BloodHound path analysis</li>
        <li>NTLM relay &amp; coercion</li><li>AD CS abuse</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="disc"><span class="wipe"></span>
      <p class="n">02</p>
      <h3>Web /<br>Exploitation</h3>
      <ul><li>Burp Suite workflow</li><li>Auth bypass logic flaws</li>
        <li>Injection &amp; SSRF</li><li>File upload chains</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="disc"><span class="wipe"></span>
      <p class="n">03</p>
      <h3>Privilege<br>Escalation</h3>
      <ul><li>SUID &amp; capabilities</li><li>cron &amp; service abuse</li>
        <li>sudo misconfiguration</li><li>Token &amp; group privesc</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="disc"><span class="wipe"></span>
      <p class="n">04</p>
      <h3>Credential<br>Attacks</h3>
      <ul><li>Hash cracking</li><li>Password spraying</li>
        <li>Credential reuse</li><li>Secrets hunting on disk</li></ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= THE PAPER ================= -->
<section class="paper">
  <p class="eyebrow">The paper · none held yet</p>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="track"></div><div class="track-fill" id="paperfill"></div>
    <div class="step now"><span class="dot"></span>
      <p class="sname">CJCA</p><p class="smeta">Exam booked</p></div>
    <div class="step later"><span class="dot"></span>
      <p class="sname">CPTS</p><p class="smeta">Next</p></div>
    <div class="step later"><span class="dot"></span>
      <p class="sname">CCNA</p><p class="smeta">Planned</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="none-held">This is the order they land in. Until then the writeups are the evidence.</p>
</section>

<!-- ================= OFF THE CLOCK ================= -->
<section class="off">
  <div class="off-grid">
    <p class="prose-k">Off the clock</p>
    <div class="off-list">
      <div class="off-item"><p class="k">Training</p>
        <p>The gym, most days. Same appeal as a box. <b>You either moved the weight or you didn't</b>,
          and no amount of talking about it changes the number.</p></div>
      <div class="off-item"><p class="k">Company</p>
        <p>A calico called <b>Laila</b> has watched more of these boxes fall than anyone
          else, and has never once been impressed.</p></div>
      <div class="off-item"><p class="k">Games</p>
        <p><b>Bloodborne</b> was my first Soulslike and it's still the one. Elden Ring is the
          most beautiful thing I've played. Both teach the same lesson as a hard box:
          the wall moves when you do.</p></div>
      <div class="off-item"><p class="k">Eye</p>
        <p>I care about <b>art and design</b> more than most people in this field. That's the
          only reason this site doesn't look like every other security portfolio.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
/* ================= OPENING ================= */
  /* No hero scene here. The type is the hero. It gets a full screen
     to itself so the page opens with a statement, not a paragraph. */
  .open{position:relative;min-height:88vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;padding:18vh 4vw 10vh}
  .open::before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;
    background:radial-gradient(ellipse 54% 62% at 14% 42%, rgba(193,31,31,.09), transparent 70%)}
  .open > *{position:relative}

  .open .eyebrow{margin:0 0 4vh;opacity:0}
  .lead{margin:0;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;
    line-height:.86;color:var(--bone)}
  /* .ln clips so each line can slide up from nothing, which means the line
     itself must never wrap, or the overflow eats it. Breaks are authored below. */
  .lead .ln{display:block;overflow:hidden}
  .lead .ln .i{display:block;white-space:nowrap;
    font-size:clamp(1.9rem,7.2vw,6.2rem);transform:translateY(104%)}
  .lead .ln.crimson .i{color:var(--blood-lit)}
  .open .slash{display:block;height:6px;width:min(22vw,260px);margin:5vh 0 4vh;
    background:var(--blood-lit);transform:scaleX(0);transform-origin:left}
  .lede{margin:0;max-width:56ch;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.82;color:#a5a19a;opacity:0}
  .lede b{color:var(--bone);font-weight:400}

  /* ================= VITALS ================= */
  .vitals{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--line);
    border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .vital{background:var(--panel);padding:30px 22px 34px;opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)}
  .vital .k{font-size:.56rem;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--blood-lit);margin:0 0 1.8em}
  .vital .v{margin:0;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;
    font-size:clamp(.95rem,1.5vw,1.3rem);line-height:1.08;color:var(--bone)}
  .vital .d{margin:.9em 0 0;font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--dim)}

  /* ================= PROSE ================= */
  .prose{padding:15vh 4vw;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .prose-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.7fr 1.3fr;gap:5vw;align-items:start}
  .prose-k{margin:0;font-size:.58rem;letter-spacing:.28em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--blood-lit)}
  /* the section runs long now, so the label rides along instead of scrolling away */
  .prose .prose-k{position:sticky;top:14vh}
  .inline{color:var(--bone);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #3a3440;
    transition:color .28s,border-color .28s}
  .inline:hover{color:var(--blood-lit);border-bottom-color:var(--blood-lit)}
  .prose em{font-style:italic;color:#a8a49c}
  /* the label and the pull quote are <p> too, and a bare `.prose p` (0,1,1)
     outranks their own classes (0,1,0), so it has to exclude them by name */
  .prose p:not(.pull):not(.prose-k){margin:0 0 1.7em;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.85;
    color:#a5a19a;max-width:66ch}
  .prose p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .prose b{color:var(--bone);font-weight:400}
  /* one line gets to be loud, because it's the thesis of the whole page */
  .pull{margin:7vh 0;padding-left:2.2vw;border-left:2px solid var(--blood-lit);
    font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;
    font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.9vw,2.3rem);line-height:1.06;color:var(--bone);max-width:22ch}

  /* ================= WHAT I ACTUALLY DO ================= */
  .kit{padding:14vh 4vw;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .kit-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--line);
    border:1px solid var(--line)}
  .disc{position:relative;background:var(--panel);padding:32px 26px 36px;overflow:hidden;
    opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)}
  .disc .wipe{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:0;height:2px;background:var(--blood-lit);
    transform:scaleX(0);transform-origin:left}
  .disc .n{margin:0;font-size:.6rem;letter-spacing:.2em;color:var(--dimmer)}
  .disc h3{margin:1.9em 0 0;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;
    font-size:clamp(1.05rem,1.9vw,1.5rem);line-height:1.02;color:var(--bone)}
  .disc ul{margin:1.5em 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none}
  .disc li{font-size:.76rem;line-height:1.5;color:var(--dim);padding:.55em 0;
    border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .disc li:first-child{border-top:0}

  /* ================= THE PAPER ================= */
  .paper{padding:14vh 4vw;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .paper .steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:0;position:relative}
  .paper .track{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:9px;height:1px;background:var(--line)}
  .paper .track-fill{position:absolute;left:0;top:9px;height:1px;background:var(--blood-lit);
    width:33.33%;transform:scaleX(0);transform-origin:left}
  .paper .step{position:relative;padding-right:24px;opacity:0}
  .paper .dot{width:19px;height:19px;border-radius:50%;border:1px solid #2a2733;
    background:var(--void);position:relative;z-index:2}
  .paper .step.now .dot{border-color:var(--blood-lit);background:var(--blood-lit);
    box-shadow:0 0 14px rgba(193,31,31,.6)}
  .paper .sname{margin:2.2em 0 .5em;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;
    font-size:clamp(1.05rem,2vw,1.6rem);color:var(--bone)}
  .paper .step.later .sname{color:#63605b}
  .paper .smeta{margin:0;font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--dimmer)}
  .paper .step.now .smeta{color:var(--blood-lit)}
  .paper .none-held{margin:5.4vh 0 0;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--dimmer)}

  /* ================= OFF THE CLOCK ================= */
  /* The one section that isn't about security. Deliberately quieter: no display
     type at scale, no accent inside the cells, so it reads as an aside, not a pitch. */
  .off{position:relative;padding:14vh 4vw 16vh}
  .off-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.7fr 1.3fr;gap:5vw;align-items:start}
  .off-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--line);
    border:1px solid var(--line)}
  .off-item{background:var(--panel);padding:28px 24px 30px;opacity:0;transform:translateY(18px)}
  .off-item .k{margin:0 0 1.4em;font-size:.56rem;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--dimmer)}
  .off-item p{margin:0;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.8;color:#a5a19a}
  .off-item b{color:var(--bone);font-weight:400}
  /* cat.glb lands here once About is built for real. See design doc. */

  @media(max-width:1000px){
    .vitals{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}
    /* The hairlines are the container background showing through 1px gaps, so
       a trailing cell with no element in it reads as a solid block of --line
       rather than as blank space. Five vitals across three columns always
       leave one. Widen the last item to close the row. Both rules stop
       applying by themselves if the count ever divides evenly by three. */
    .vitals > *:last-child:nth-child(3n+1){grid-column:span 3}
    .vitals > *:last-child:nth-child(3n+2){grid-column:span 2}
    .kit-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}
  }
  @media(max-width:820px){
    .prose-grid,.off-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4vh}
    .paper .steps{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:3.4vh}
    .paper .track,.paper .track-fill{display:none}
    .off-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  }
  @media(max-width:560px){
    .vitals{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .kit-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  }
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
    .lead .ln .i{transform:none}
    .open .eyebrow,.lede,.vital,.disc,.off-item,.paper .step{opacity:1;transform:none}
  }
</style>

<script>
import gsap from 'gsap';
import ScrollTrigger from 'gsap/ScrollTrigger';
gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);

/* nav only earns a background once you've left the opening */
const nav = document.getElementById('nav');
const onScroll = () => nav.classList.toggle('stuck', window.scrollY > 40);
onScroll(); addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, {passive:true});

if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
  /* everything is already visible via the CSS media query, nothing to animate */
} else {
  /* opening: the headline arrives line by line, same percussion as the hero */
  gsap.timeline({delay:.15})
    .to('.open .eyebrow',{opacity:1,duration:.5,ease:'power2.out'})
    .to('.lead .ln .i',{y:'0%',duration:.82,ease:'power4.out',stagger:.085},'-=.28')
    .to('.slash',{scaleX:1,duration:.5,ease:'power4.out'},'-=.34')
    .to('.lede',{opacity:1,duration:.7,ease:'power2.out'},'-=.3');

  gsap.to('.vital',{opacity:1,y:0,duration:.5,ease:'power4.out',stagger:.07,
    scrollTrigger:{trigger:'.vitals',start:'top 88%'}});

  gsap.utils.toArray('.disc').forEach((el,i)=>{
    gsap.timeline({scrollTrigger:{trigger:el,start:'top 88%'}})
      .to(el,{opacity:1,y:0,duration:.55,ease:'power4.out',delay:i*.06})
      .to(el.querySelector('.wipe'),{scaleX:1,duration:.5,ease:'power3.inOut'},'-=.34');
  });

  gsap.timeline({scrollTrigger:{trigger:'.paper',start:'top 80%'}})
    .to('.paper .step',{opacity:1,duration:.45,ease:'power4.out',stagger:.11})
    .to('#paperfill',{scaleX:1,duration:.8,ease:'power3.inOut'},'-=.45');

  gsap.to('.off-item',{opacity:1,y:0,duration:.5,ease:'power4.out',stagger:.07,
    scrollTrigger:{trigger:'.off',start:'top 84%'}});

  gsap.timeline({scrollTrigger:{trigger:'.foot',start:'top 85%'}})
    .from('.foot-k',{opacity:0,y:12,duration:.3,ease:'power4.out'})
    .from('.foot-mail',{opacity:0,y:20,duration:.36,ease:'power4.out'},'-=.14')
    .from('.foot-note',{opacity:0,duration:.5},'-=.2')
    .from('.foot-links a,.foot-flat',{opacity:0,x:16,duration:.28,ease:'power4.out',stagger:.06},'-=.34')
    .from('.foot-base',{opacity:0,duration:.4},'-=.1')
    .from('.foot-mark',{opacity:0,y:34,duration:.8,ease:'power3.out'},'-=.25')
    .from('.totop',{opacity:0,scale:.8,duration:.4,ease:'back.out(2)'},'-=.8');
}
</script>
